A weeknight dinner lifesaver that delivers deep teriyaki flavor in under 30 minutes. Made without bottled high-fructose sauces, this recipe uses pantry-standard soy sauce, brown sugar, mirin, sake, and fresh garlic. Pressure cooking keeps lean chicken breasts succulent and moist, while a quick post-cook cornstarch simmer thickens the cooking liquid into a lustrous restaurant glaze.

*Adapted from [Allrecipes](https://www.allrecipes.com/recipe/262228/instant-pot-teriyaki-chicken-breast/).*

## Ingredients

### Homemade Teriyaki Sauce
- ½ cup low-sodium soy sauce
- ½ cup water
- ½ cup packed brown sugar
- 2 tablespoons rice wine vinegar
- 1 tablespoon mirin (Japanese sweet cooking wine)
- 1 tablespoon cooking sake (or dry sherry, or additional water)
- 1 tablespoon garlic, finely minced
- 1 dash freshly cracked black pepper

### Chicken & Thickener
- 1 lb boneless, skinless chicken breasts (or boneless chicken thighs)
- 1 tablespoon cornstarch
- 1 tablespoon cold water

### For Garnish & Serving
- 1 teaspoon toasted white sesame seeds
- 2 scallions, thinly sliced on the diagonal
- Steamed Jasmine or Calrose rice
- Steamed fresh broccoli florets

## Instructions

1. **Whisk the Teriyaki Sauce:** In a bowl or measuring cup, combine the soy sauce, water, brown sugar, rice wine vinegar, mirin, sake, minced garlic, and black pepper. Whisk until the brown sugar has completely dissolved into the sauce.
2. **Add to Instant Pot:** Lay the raw chicken breasts flat in the inner pot of your Instant Pot. Pour the teriyaki sauce directly over the chicken, making sure the meat is submerged in the marinade.
3. **Pressure Cook on High:** Secure the Instant Pot lid and turn the steam valve to **Sealing**. Select **Manual / Pressure Cook** on **HIGH** pressure and set the time for **8 minutes** (if your chicken breasts are unusually thick, use 10 minutes).
4. **Quick Pressure Release:** As soon as the cook cycle beeps, carefully perform a quick pressure release by moving the valve to **Venting**. When the float valve drops, unlock and remove the lid.
5. **Rest and Slice Chicken:** Use tongs to transfer the cooked chicken breasts to a cutting board. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 165°F (74°C). Let the chicken rest for 3 to 5 minutes so the juices redistribute, then slice into ½-inch strips or shred using two forks.
6. **Thicken the Teriyaki Glaze:** Press **Cancel**, then select **Sauté** on the Instant Pot. In a small cup, stir the 1 tablespoon cornstarch with 1 tablespoon cold water until dissolved into a slurry. Whisk the slurry directly into the simmering sauce in the pot. Cook at a gentle boil for 2 to 3 minutes, stirring constantly with a whisk, until the sauce clarifies, darkens, and thickens into a rich, glossy glaze. Press Cancel.
7. **Assemble and Garnish:** Return the sliced or shredded chicken to the pot and gently toss until every piece is coated in the sticky teriyaki glaze. Spoon over bowls of steamed white rice and tender broccoli florets, drizzling extra pan glaze on top. Garnish with toasted sesame seeds and sliced scallions.

## Notes

- **Chicken Thighs:** Boneless, skinless chicken thighs make an even juicier alternative; pressure cook for 8 minutes and follow the exact same glaze-thickening steps.
- **Meal Prep Friendly:** Portions hold exceptionally well in airtight meal prep containers in the refrigerator for up to 4 days.
